# ternary-bonsai/.gitignore - THE LARGE FILES ONLY
#
# The navigator's rule, 2026-09-20: "we keep the weights in there locally, but gitignored"
# and "the final weights we make too all gitignored, the large files only".
#
# So this file ignores BY EXTENSION, never by wildcarding a directory. Every small thing
# inside an artifact directory stays TRACKED: its README.md, its INDEX.md, its .gitkeep,
# its run manifests, its checksum files, its configs, its logs. A gitignored tree clones
# as nothing, so the SKELETON has to survive a fresh clone or the next person rebuilds a
# different structure.
#
# Checked against the repo root .gitignore before writing: that file ignores /gguf and
# models/ and neither rule reaches ternary-bonsai/, verified with
#   git check-ignore -v ternary-bonsai/artifacts/ternary-gguf/     -> exit 1, no rule
#   git check-ignore -v gguf/                                      -> exit 0, .gitignore:12
# so this is a new rule and not a second overlapping one.

# model weights and quantised outputs
*.safetensors
*.gguf
*.ggml
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt

# calibration matrices and captured tensors
*.imatrix
*.npy
*.npz
*.dat

# archives that would carry any of the above
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tar.zst
*.tgz
*.zip
*.7z

# NOT ignored, deliberately, because they are small and they are the ledger:
#   *.md  *.json  *.csv  *.txt  *.sha256  *.log  *.sh  *.py  .gitkeep
# A safetensors shard index (model.safetensors.index.json) is a few hundred KB of JSON
# and is the file that answers the P0 subset question. It stays tracked.
